\title{The regex tree has a variant for once or more}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-17}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{stdlib}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1086}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The public enum \code{\verb~|Regex~} gains the variant \code{\verb~|Plus~}, and \code{\verb~|Regex::plus~} builds it, where it built the operand followed by its star and so held the operand twice. The operand is translated to bytes once. Code that matches on \code{\verb~|Regex~} without a catch-all arm needs an arm for it; in the library only the translation does. See [the session](ses-A1OD).}

\p{Merged as \pr{1086}.}
